IMSD: make the 0x23 link-up reply selectable, parse its payload.

The DPM.2.0.2 modem announces an IMS link with IMSD 0x23 instead of the
documented 0x20 Start Connection.  Decode the announcement, remember the
connection id it carries, and let the reply be chosen with
IMSD_LINKUP_REPLY so both hypotheses can be tested without a rebuild:

  down (default)  reply err_code 13 ("connection down") and do not start
                  the "ims" PDN ourselves, so the modem has to send 0x20.
  up              reply success and start the PDN after 90 s (old path).

When the PDN is started from the link-up path it is registered with
connection 0, so report the id from 0x23 in the connection-changed
indication instead -- the modem ignores an indication for a connection it
does not track.

